-----------------------------------------------------------------------
AI Security Risk Workbook (Jason Robbins)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Handrail builds on the AI Security Risk Workbook v3.0 by Jason
Robbins (https://github.com/jasonmichaelrobbins-arch/-ai-security-governance-workbook,
commit b775ec31a34e7788bb5b75fc55111d5a51d991b2), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

These files are modified from that workbook. Each states what was
changed:

  - data/functions.yaml, data/controls.yaml and the files in
    data/crosswalks/ (the function and guardrail catalog and its mappings),
    and their copies in plugin/skills/handrail-assessor/data/
    (functions.yaml, controls.yaml, owasp.yaml)
  - kit/crosswalk.xlsx and docs/crosswalk.md, generated from those files
  - data/model.yaml (level wording for six capability and data questions,
    the data classes, and the default routing roles, which follow the
    workbook's Org Profile starter values), and its copies in
    plugin/skills/*/data/. The same level wording and routing roles appear
    in kit/scoring-rubric.md, kit/quick-score-worksheet.md and
    docs/level-1.md (inside the blocks marked <!-- rubric: ... -->),
    kit/policy.md section 10, kit/profile.yaml, examples/saas-company/
    profile.yaml and plugin/skills/handrail-advisor/data/profile.yaml;
    that wording remains Apache-2.0 within those files
  - control names and identifiers, and function identifiers, used in
    examples/saas-company/*.record.md (from data/controls.yaml and
    data/functions.yaml)
  - plugin/skills/handrail-assessor/SKILL.md (from the
    ai-tool-risk-assessment skill: ground rules and record structure)
  - kit/assessment-record.md (from that skill's record format), and its
    copy in plugin/skills/handrail-assessor/data/
  - kit/intake-form.md (from the AI Intake Form and that skill's
    internal-build block)
  - tools/check (record rules reimplemented from that skill)

The function and guardrail identifiers (for example POS-01, NHI-07) are
identifiers from the workbook, kept for traceability. They are not a
published industry standard.

